! ax4b_1a_ifield_select.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 148 (1248,
! "INDEX MODIFICATION TEST", banner PDF p.113: "TEST1. BASIC TESTS
! INCLUDING I FIELD INDEX SELECTION ..."), TEST 1A "I-FLD IX SELN.":
!
!   PDF p.114  007441.00-007475.00  I481, I482: IX 0, 1, 2
!   PDF p.115  007475.40-007500.40  IX 2 (end)
!   PDF p.116  007501.00-007534.40  IX 3, exit, I483: IX 4, 5
!   PDF p.117  007535.00-007570.40  IX 6, 7, exit, I484: IX 8
!   PDF p.118  007571.00-007624.40  IX 9, 10, 11, exit
!   PDF p.119  007625.00-007654.40  I485: IX 12, 13, 14
!   PDF p.120  007655.00-007670.40  IX 15, exit
!   PDF p.152  011310.00-011320.00  148S1 (clear all IX regs), 148S2
!   PDF p.153  011320.40-011340.40  CNOP, 148K0-148K15
!   PDF p.153  011372.00            148ER1
!   PDF p.154  011373.00            148DMP
!   PDF p.190  013036.00            100VO
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi; checked row for row
! against the printed machine code by
! tests/verify_ax4b_1a_ifield_select_listing.py.
!
! WHAT IT TESTS (IBM's code, unchanged).  148Kn is not a constant but an
! INSTRUCTION, "SX,$Xn,148DMP" (p.153); "LX,$Xn,148Kn" loads that
! half-word pair as an index word, so Xn's value is 148DMP's address
! with Xn's own number in the low bits (11373.01 for X0 ... 11373.37
! for X15).  Then, for each n:
!   148S1 clears all sixteen index registers; LX,$Xn,148Kn; Z,148DMP;
!   SX,$Xn,0($Xn)    I = n: the effective address is Xn's value, i.e.
!                    148DMP -- the store must land there (BZRZ: 148DMP
!                    nonzero), "NO IX MODIFICATION WHEN I FIELD IS n."
! IX 0 is the exception: all sixteen registers are loaded, and
!   SX,$X0,0($X0)    0.01 10 -- I = 0 means NO indexing, so the store
!                    goes to word 0, not 148DMP, and 148DMP must stay
!                    ZERO (BRZ), "IX MODIFICATION WHEN I FIELD IS 0."
! A failure halts at SERS (below) with SIC's link in SEN; IBM's own code
! would then store 100VO into 148ER1 ("STORE ERROR INDICATOR"), which
! later tests read; on a pass 148ER1 stays as I481 cleared it.
!
! FOUR SEGMENTS.  Each group of four (I482: IX 0-3, I483: 4-7, I484:
! 8-11, I485: 12-15) ends in its own "B,SSW" (TO SSIP).  With SSW a PASS
! halt, one run covers one group, so the driver runs this deck four
! times: from END (I481) and with ENTRY=I483, I484, I485 (gen_tb.py's
! ENTRY=, added for these segments).  Each group's continuity rows after
! its B,SSW are transcribed and verified but never run.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points: SSW (001301.00) is a PASS halt, SERS
!     (001304.00) a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO (001310.00/001311.00) data words
!     SIC stores into.  The addresses are the listing's own (B,SSW
!     prints "1301.10 00", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SEN "1310.00 80",
!     SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80"); the contents are SSIP's, which is not
!     transcribed.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41, PDF 44),
!     so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the error entry on a failure.
!   * IC248 and BIT0-BIT3 are SYN'd from the printed "LX,$X13,IC248"
!     (11306.32 10) and "V+,$X13,BITk" (13054.32 B0 ... 13057.32 B0);
!     the continuity rows that name them are never run.
!   * Notation only: the page's "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")";
!     the label glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I48..,
!     I00VO), as for every ax4b label (docs/listing_typography.md).  The
!     listing's second NOP of each pair is printed indented; STRAP
!     ignores that.  Nothing else changed.
!
! RESULT, 2026-11-19: every segment halts at SSW (PASS, PC 1410) with
! SEN = 0.  The driver compares PC, SEN, CYCLES and the pins listed in
! tests/run_tests.sh; CYCLES is MODEL BEHAVIOUR, not IBM's timing.
! SEN, on a failure, is SIC's link: the half-word after the "B,SERS" that
! was taken, so it names the failing check.
! MODEL INJECTIONS, OBSERVED (each built in its own scratch copy of
! stretch/bsv/, all 19 segment runs of TESTs 1-2 repeated; the
! worktree's bsv/ was never edited):
!   effAddrSigned reads index register (idx & 7), so I = 8..15 index by
!     X0..X7 -> I484 FAIL halt, SEN 007570.00 (IX 8's B,SERS), CYCLES
!     318, 148DMP 0; I485 FAIL halt, SEN 007634.00 (IX 12), CYCLES 318.
!     I481 and I483 (IX 0-7) PASS, as they must; none of the other
!     runs of these five decks moves.
!   I = 0 indexed by X0 (effAddrSigned's idx == 0 case removed) ->
!     I481 FAIL halt (PC 1416), 148DMP 0, CYCLES 613; SEN stays 0 --
!     INFERRED, not dumped: SIC,SEN (I = 0) is then itself indexed by X0
!     and stores elsewhere, as in ax4b_5i_prog_ix_x0.
!   I = 1..7 read X(I+8) (readIndex(idx | 8)) -> I481 FAIL halt, SEN
!     007470.00 (IX 1's B,SERS), CYCLES 880; I483 FAIL halt, SEN
!     007524.00 (IX 4), CYCLES 318.
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model in the same scratch arrangement: all
!     19 runs PASS with the pins in run_tests.sh.
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! IC248, BIT0-BIT3: SYN from the printed continuity rows (never run).
IC248   SYN, (8)11306.0
BIT0    SYN, (8)13054.0
BIT1    SYN, (8)13055.0
BIT2    SYN, (8)13056.0
BIT3    SYN, (8)13057.0
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.114, 007441.00-007475.00 (no printed page number on the sheet)
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)7441.0
!                                     -TEST1A I-FLD IX SELN.
I481    Z,   I48ER1                   ! -CLEAR ERROR INDICATOR REGISTER.
I482    SIC, I48S2                    ! -CHK I-FLD SELN FOR IX 0.
        B,   I48S1                    ! -GO CLEAR ALL INDEX REGS.
        LX,  $X0, I48K0
        LX,  $X1, I48K1
        LX,  $X2, I48K2
        LX,  $X3, I48K3
        LX,  $X4, I48K4
        LX,  $X5, I48K5
        LX,  $X6, I48K6
        LX,  $X7, I48K7
        LX,  $X8, I48K8
        LX,  $X9, I48K9
        LX,  $X10, I48K10
        LX,  $X11, I48K11
        LX,  $X12, I48K12
        LX,  $X13, I48K13
        LX,  $X14, I48K14
        LX,  $X15, I48K15
        Z,   I48DMP
        NOP
        NOP
        SX,  $X0, 0($X0)
        NOP
        NOP
        L(BU), I48DMP
        BRZ, $+2.32
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IX MODIFICATION WHEN
        B,   SERS                     ! -I FIELD IS 0.
        LX,  $X1, I00VO               ! -STORE ERROR INDICATOR.
        SX,  $X1, I48ER1
        SIC, I48S2                    ! -CHK I-FLD SELN FOR IX 1.
        B,   I48S1                    ! -GO CLEAR ALL INDEX REGS.
        LX,  $X1, I48K1
        Z,   I48DMP
        NOP
        NOP
        SX,  $X1, 0($X1)
        NOP
        NOP
        L(BU), I48DMP
        BZRZ, $+2.32
        SIC, SEN                      ! -NO IX MODIFICATION WHEN
        B,   SERS                     ! -I FIELD IS 1.
        LX,  $X1, I00VO               ! -STORE ERROR INDICATOR.
        SX,  $X1, I48ER1
        SIC, I48S2                    ! -CHK I-FLD SELN FOR IX 2.
        B,   I48S1                    ! -GO CLEAR ALL INDEX REGS.
        LX,  $X2, I48K2
        Z,   I48DMP
        NOP
        NOP
        SX,  $X2, 0($X2)
        NOP
        NOP
! ---- PDF p.115, 007475.40-007500.40 ----
        L(BU), I48DMP
        BZRZ, $+2.32
        SIC, SEN                      ! -NO IX MODIFICATION WHEN
        B,   SERS                     ! -I FIELD IS 2.
        LX,  $X1, I00VO               ! -STORE ERROR INDICATOR.
